From 6fab15e32bc3041d7fe65b9900617fd92aa9a3c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JavaZeroo <2487163254@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 01:44:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: implement aten::_flash_attention_forward/_backward on
 npu_fusion_attention

torch.nn.attention.varlen.varlen_attn (and the SDPA flash path) lower to
aten::_flash_attention_forward / _backward, which have no PrivateUse1
kernel:

  NotImplementedError: Could not run 'aten::_flash_attention_forward' ...

Callers written against the public flash-attention contract -- e.g.
torchtitan's VarlenAttention -- therefore cannot run on Ascend.

Register PrivateUse1 implementations backed by npu_fusion_attention /
npu_fusion_attention_grad: dense (B,S,N,D) and packed varlen (T,N,D)
layouts, right-aligned causal (sparse_mode 3), left window (sparse_mode 4),
GQA. The kernel's per-sequence head-major softmax statistics are folded
into the aten logsumexp layout ((B,N,S) / (N,T)) and expanded back for the
backward with softmax_sum == 1, which satisfies the kernel's
P = exp(S - max) / sum. Dropout, alibi, paged KV and seqused_k are rejected
explicitly.

Validated on Ascend 910B2 / CANN 9.1.0 with torch 2.15.0.dev20260812 +
torch_npu master: varlen_attn forward and grads match a fp32 reference per
document (bf16 tolerance), and torchtitan's stock VarlenAttention model
trains.

Test: test/npu/test_flash_attention_privateuse1.py (registration, dense
causal forward vs reference, varlen MHA/GQA forward + backward vs
reference, unsupported features raise).

Upstream-PR: https://gitcode.com/Ascend/pytorch/merge_requests/45527
Upstream-Issue: https://gitcode.com/Ascend/pytorch/issues/4439
